#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:0
msgid ""
"Upgrade your Ubuntu installation to the next release, including supported "
"upgrade paths from LTS and interim versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:9
msgid "Topics: Updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:13
msgid "Upgrade Ubuntu Desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:15
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Originally, this comes from a Tutorial and a Community Help Wiki pages:\n"
"\n"
"https://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop/14012\n"
"Author \tOliver Smith oliversmith@canonical.com\n"
"\n"
"https://help.ubuntu.com/community/QuestingUpgrades/\n"
"https://help.ubuntu.com/community/UpgradeNotes\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:25
msgid ""
"You can upgrade your Ubuntu installation when a new version comes out. The "
"upgrade process is interactive and takes up to an hour, depending on your "
"internet connection speed and computer performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:27
msgid ""
"You benefit from getting the latest software, including new security "
"patches, and all the upgraded technology that comes with a new release "
"without having to reinstall and reconfigure your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:30
msgid ""
"If you're upgrading from a very outdated release, you might have to repeat "
"the upgrade process several times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:32
msgid ""
"Ubuntu only supports sequential upgrades: from one Long Term Support (LTS) "
"release to the next, or from one interim release to the next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:36
msgid "Latest releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:38
msgid "Your Ubuntu installation follows one of these upgrade paths:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:40
msgid ""
"If you're using a **Long Term Support (LTS) release** like most of Ubuntu "
"users, the latest version that you can upgrade to is [Ubuntu 26.04 LTS]"
"(https://documentation.ubuntu.com/release-notes/26.04/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:42
msgid ""
"Upgrades to the latest LTS release become available after the first point "
"release, such as with Ubuntu 26.04.01. This usually happens several months "
"after the initial release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:44
msgid ""
"If you're using **interim releases**, you can upgrade to [Ubuntu 26.10]"
"(https://documentation.ubuntu.com/release-notes/26.10/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:46
msgid ""
"Upgrades to the latest interim release become available a few days after the "
"official release date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:48
msgid ""
"If you want to upgrade from an LTS release to an interim release, see {ref}"
"`switch-between-an-lts-and-interim-release`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:51
msgid "Prepare for the upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:53
msgid ""
"If you're using a laptop or a mobile device, make sure that it's **plugged "
"into a power source**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:55
msgid ""
"Check that there is **enough free disk space**. Ubuntu needs to store "
"several gigabytes of data during the upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:57
msgid ""
"**Back up** all of your user data to an external storage device. Although "
"it's unlikely that data will be lost during the upgrade process, it's better "
"to be safe than sorry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:59
msgid "Make sure that your current Ubuntu installation is fully **updated**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:0
msgid "Graphical interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:66
#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:114
msgid "Open the Software Updater application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:67
msgid "If any updates are available, install them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:68
msgid "Restart your computer if prompted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:0
msgid "Command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:74
msgid "Refresh package information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:84
msgid "Install updates:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:94
msgid "Restart your computer if prompted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:105
msgid "Start the upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:107
msgid "Start the application that upgrades your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:116
msgid "The application informs you that a new release is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:118
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Upgrade`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:133
msgid ""
"If no upgrade is available, you're either on the latest version of Ubuntu or "
"upgrades to the latest release haven't been enabled yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:135
msgid ""
"The process is interactive. Follow the application's instructions and "
"confirm the prompts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:137
msgid ""
"The application presents an **overview** of the upgrade, including a link to "
"the release notes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:139
msgid ""
"When all upgrade requirements have been gathered, the application shows an "
"overview of the **packages** to be installed and removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:141
msgid ""
"If you installed packages from Personal Package Archives (PPAs) or third-"
"party repositories, the **Foreign Packages Installed** prompt opens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:143
msgid ""
"You can try to proceed with the upgrade. If the upgrade fails, remove the "
"packages manually and try the upgrade again. When you log into the upgraded "
"system later, reinstall the third-party packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:145
msgid ""
"While the upgrade is in progress, you might see visual **glitches** on your "
"screen, such as changing icons. This is normal. Wait until the process is "
"complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:147
msgid ""
"When new packages have been installed, the application prompts you to remove "
"the **obsolete packages** from the previous Ubuntu release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:149
msgid ""
"Unless you have a reason to keep the packages, it's best to remove them. "
"This usually takes a minute or two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:151
msgid "When the upgrade is complete, **restart** your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:154
msgid "Finalize the upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:156
msgid ""
"Your new, upgraded Ubuntu starts up. Log in and check that everything works "
"as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:158
msgid ""
"Third-party software repositories and PPAs might have been disabled during "
"the release upgrade. Check if you need to re-enable them or find updated "
"versions. You can do this in the Software & Updates application, on the "
"{guilabel}`Other Software` tab. If the application is missing on your "
"system, you can install it from the `software-properties-gtk` Deb package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:161
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:163
msgid "You might encounter these problems when trying to upgrade Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:165
msgid "The upgrade isn't available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:167
msgid ""
"LTS upgrades only become available with the first point release, such as "
"26.04.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:169
msgid ""
"Upgrades to the latest interim release become available several days after "
"the official release date. This is to allow time for any critical bugs to be "
"fixed before prompting all users to upgrade. Check again in a few days. If "
"it's been more than a couple of days, look for known issues in the release "
"notes. Some of them might be blocking the upgrade until they're resolved. "
"You can find updates in the attached bug trackers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:171
msgid ""
"If you want to upgrade to an interim release, make sure that your system is "
"{ref}`properly configured <switch-between-an-lts-and-interim-release>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:173
msgid "You can force the upgrade manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:201
msgid ""
"If the normal upgrade path isn't available yet and you know what you're "
"doing, you can also add the `--devel-release` option to upgrade to the "
"latest development release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:230
msgid ""
"Upgrading to a development release isn't supported and might break your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:233
msgid "The system is slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:235
msgid ""
"Your machine might be slow to reboot right after the upgrade because it "
"still needs to complete the initial configuration. After that, it should be "
"back to normal speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:237
msgid ""
"If it seems that the new Ubuntu release is much slower than the previous "
"one, check the system requirements in the release notes to make sure that "
"your hardware is still supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:239
msgid ""
"You can also {ref}`reinstall Ubuntu <install-ubuntu-desktop>` from scratch "
"to get a clean system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:241
msgid ""
"You can return to an earlier LTS release by reinstalling Ubuntu. Downgrading "
"the existing system isn't supported. Make sure that the release that you "
"choose still receives security updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:244
msgid ""
"To extend the support lifetime of your Ubuntu LTS system, consider enabling "
"[Ubuntu Pro](https://ubuntu.com/pro) in the Security Center. You also "
"receive security updates to community-maintained packages and get access to "
"certain enterprise features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:246
msgid "Ubuntu Pro is free for personal use on up to 5 machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:249
msgid ""
"Consider [Ubuntu flavors](https://ubuntu.com/desktop/flavors). These are "
"community projects that provide alternative desktop environments and default "
"applications. They might run better on older hardware while still being "
"based on the latest Ubuntu release. However, flavors aren't supported by "
"Canonical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:251
msgid "The system powered off during the upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:253
msgid ""
"If  your computer lost power during the upgrade, try to start it again. It "
"might be able to resume the upgrade process. Log in and try to fix any "
"broken packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:255
msgid "Configure unpacked updates:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:265
msgid "Fix broken dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/upgrade-ubuntu-desktop.md:275
msgid ""
"If you can't log in or the these steps didn't work, it's best to ask for "
"help on the Ubuntu support channels. See {ref}`project-and-community`."
msgstr ""
